## What's happening?
The Collector `memory_limiter` processor `{{processor.name}}` refused **{{value}} records** during the last 15 minutes. This signal is shared across every destination the Collector ships to, not just BYOC, because `memory_limiter` reads process-wide heap: it does not prove the BYOC path caused the pressure. Use the exporter queue comparison to attribute it. Whether this costs data depends on how logs reach the Collector: a pushed OTLP client loses data unless it retries, while a `filelog` receiver simply stops advancing its read offset and loses nothing until log rotation outruns it.
{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_recovery}}`memory_limiter` processor `{{processor.name}}` stopped refusing data.{{/is_recovery}}

